+# Local resource access
+
+The Local resources form sends a GET request directly from the user's browser to
+the supplied device or companion app URL. Choose the network device option for
+LAN addresses (including `.local` names), or the computer option for `localhost`,
+`127.0.0.1`, or `[::1]`. No request is sent until Connect is clicked.
+
+Deploy the site over HTTPS. The local service must return a standard
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header allowing the deployed site's origin. Browser
+permission does not replace CORS. The service must support requests without
+cookies or embedded URL credentials. Redirects are deliberately rejected.
+
+Requests declare `targetAddressSpace` as `local` or `loopback`. Browsers supporting
+Local Network Access prompt for permission; unsupported permission queries fall
+back to connecting on click, subject to that browser's security restrictions.
+Browsers without the HTTP mixed-content exemption may require the resource to
+use HTTPS. Deprecated Private Network Access preflight headers are not needed.
+
+If hosting policies are configured, allow this origin to use
+`local-network=(self), loopback-network=(self)` in the `Permissions-Policy` header
+and allow the intended endpoints in CSP `connect-src`. These permissions default
+to self when no policy overrides them. When embedding this site cross-origin,
+the parent must also delegate `local-network; loopback-network` through the
+iframe's `allow` attribute and its own response policy. The child cannot override
+a restrictive parent policy.
